{
  "label": "The problem and how Tezera solves it",
  "before": {
    "kicker": "The problem",
    "heading": "The people exist. Finding them doesn't.",
    "body": "Caterers, crews and stall-holders are out there, but they're spread across group chats, phone books and old flyers. Organisers spend weeks chasing, good vendors wait to be found, and the crowd misses what's on."
  },
  "after": {
    "kicker": "How Tezera solves it",
    "heading": "One stage for the whole show.",
    "body": "Organisers hire verified vendors and freelancers, fill stalls and share the venue map. Attendees find what's on and who's going. Every finished job leaves a review the next organiser can read, so work is won on track record, not contacts."
  },
